<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhenish-German National Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1793">1793</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rhenish-German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> was an assembly elected under French supervision in the territories on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-occupation-of-the-netherlands">French revolutionary armies</a>. Meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> from 17 March 1793, it proclaimed a free state from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landau">Landau</a> to Bingen, known as the Republic of Mainz, and days later asked for union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It is regarded as the first parliament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> elected on democratic principles; Prussian forces retook Mainz in July 1793.</p></div>
